{"name":"Risotto","hex":"#f8f5e9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"risotto","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An Italian savoury dish made with rice and other ingredients.","A similar dish made without rice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/risotto"}],"entries":[{"title":"Risotto","blocks":[{"text":"Risotto is an Italian rice dish cooked with broth until it reaches a creamy consistency. The broth can be derived from meat, fish or vegetables. Many types of risotto contain butter, onion, white wine, and Parmesan cheese. It is one of the most common ways of cooking rice in Italy. Saffron was originally used for flavour and its signature yellow colour."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Risotto_with_speck_and_goat_cheese_%286101067436%29.jpg/330px-Risotto_with_speck_and_goat_cheese_%286101067436%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Risotto","wikidata":"Q208105"},{"title":"Risotto (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Risotto is the fourth studio album by British electronica group Fluke, released on 30 September 1997 on Circa Records, and on Astralwerks in the US. It was the band's last album recorded with Mike Tournier."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/11/Risotto_%28Fluke_album_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Risotto_(album)","wikidata":"Q7336336"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Risotto_giallo_%286954045202%29.jpg/500px-Risotto_giallo_%286954045202%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Risotto_giallo_%286954045202%29.jpg/500px-Risotto_giallo_%286954045202%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","lin